  Findings and work left undone
  - env-example: The secret scan flags lang/strings_portuguese_standard.txt ($s_password = 'Palavra-chave', a translated UI label). This is a false positive. The file comes from translatewiki.net and agents must not edit it, so env-example stays partial.
  - ci: `npx -y uw-harness verify` returned 404 from the npm registry during this build: the package is not published yet. The new workflow .github/workflows/harness.yml will fail until uw-harness is on npm. I checked locally with the CLI from a local checkout (`check` passes).
  - fast-gate: build/check_lineterm.php is not in the lint. It always exits 0 and scans vendor/ and node_modules/. git ls-files --eol shows two vendored files with CRLF or mixed line endings (css/bootstrap-datetimepicker-4.17.49.min.css, library/rssbuilder/class.RSS_V_200.inc.php). I left them unchanged because they are product and vendored code.
  - full-gate: The local gates cover MySQL and the local PHP version only (8.5.3 on this machine). PostgreSQL, the PHP 8.1 to 8.6 matrix and the DocBook/Publican build stay in the existing CI workflows.

